    "explanation": "28 birds are annotated and Faster R-CNN reports 40, an overcount of +12, of which 14 are false alarms. Classified by cause, 0 overlap the box of a bird already found, 1 sits on a bird whose credit went to a detection further away, 6 sit on no annotated bird but are reported by all 8 models, and 7 are reported by no other model. The swapped case is what appears in the panel as one bird detected twice. The model placed a detection on the bird, and placed a second, higher-scoring detection on something else nearby. Matching proceeds in order of confidence and accepts any bird within 40 px, which is about 2.3 times the width of a bird here, so the higher-scoring detection claimed the bird first and the detection sitting on it was left as the false alarm. The dashed line in the panel joins the bird to the detection that received the credit. No false alarm overlaps a detection of the same bird, so non-maximum suppression is not the cause of the overcount. Recorded at habitat WaterVegetation, 89 m, cloud, Bird_G.",
