    "explanation": "11 birds are annotated in this crop and Faster R-CNN finds every one of them, yet it reports 45 detections in total, an overcount of +34. Of the 34 detections matching no annotated bird, 33 fall within the matching radius of a detection from every one of the 8 models, at a median confidence of 0.994. Those models differ in architecture, in training regime and in whether they predict boxes or points. Agreement of that kind is not readily explained by eight independent false positives landing on the same coordinates, and the more economical reading is that the crop is under-annotated: the birds are present and were not labelled. The consequence is that precision is understated wherever this occurs, for every model, because a correct detection of an unlabelled bird is scored as an error. Section 7.5 reports how often the pattern appears across the test split. Recorded at 90 m, Bird_D.",
